# ==== T-FMT-B — the NINTH name-string cell: `AttributeArg::KeyValue`'s
# BARE-IDENTIFIER producer (`src/parser/mod.rs`, the `expect_identifier` arm of
# the `key = value` branch).
# SCOPE CLAIM: this cell pins that a bare-identifier attribute VALUE stays
# BARE. Pre-fix RED (measured): the emitter QUOTED it unconditionally
# (`unit = ms` -> `unit = "ms"`), inventing a string where the author wrote an
# identifier — a form change the reparse gate cannot see because the quoted
# form re-parses fine as the OTHER producer.
# `@timeout` is used rather than `@inline` because `@inline` is semantically
# rejected; `@timeout(unit = ms)` parses AND checks clean.
@timeout(unit = ms)
void decorated():
    print(1)

void main():
    decorated()
